notes.body:
Here's what the new icon looks like on Tahoe with the default, dark, clear, and tinted themes along with the VS Code and Terminal icons for comparison:

![wireshark-lg-default](/uploads/1308886ca879811588f8cecd995d49e1/wireshark-lg-default.png){width=198 height=86}
![wireshark-lg-dark](/uploads/53f1238e3bfd81d66a3024bcfe3097e7/wireshark-lg-dark.png){width=201 height=87}
![wireshark-lg-clear](/uploads/3d0e3d1f5e69275ec659a2a981c3fd23/wireshark-lg-clear.png){width=196 height=87}
![wireshark-lg-tinted](/uploads/7fcb4dc757879e96ff3e56cba47eda84/wireshark-lg-tinted.png){width=209 height=84}

Here's what things look like while a capture is in progress. Unfortunately I haven't figured out how to apply any non-default themes:

![wireshark-lg-default-caputre](/uploads/98fb7fb874ffb5384f8f861c2f9d87e8/wireshark-lg-default-caputre.png){width=198 height=86}

Here's what the new plain and capture icons look like on Sonoma:

![wireshark-classic](/uploads/81ce397a2d1326360388bf79735294fe/wireshark-classic.png){width=294 height=128}

![wireshark-classic-capture](/uploads/74bc2b6f6b16197f3d550fd38898ae08/wireshark-classic-capture.png){width=288 height=130}

